        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.121,
            0.736,
            0.142
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 1",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " announces to all, an angle measure, e.g., 34°."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.149,
            0.835,
            0.218
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A player from Team 2 must draw that angle on the board without using a protractor. Other members of "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 2",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can help the player by speaking words like ‘Make it bigger!’ or ‘Make it smaller!’."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.223,
            0.834,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• A player from "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 1",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " measures the angle with a protractor for all to see."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.274,
            0.835,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 2 scores the number of points that is the absolute difference in degrees between "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 2",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "’s angle size and the intended angle size. For example, if player’s angle from "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team  2",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is measured to be 25°, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Team 2",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " scores 9 points (34°–25°)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.371,
            0.833,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Each team gets five turns. The winner is again the team with the lowest score."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.403,
            0.428,
            0.572,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Teacher’s Note"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.448,
            0.801,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "These games are important to play to build intuition about angles and their measures. Return to this game at least once or twice on different days to build practice in estimating angles. Note that these games can also be played between pairs of students."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
